      "text": "Given the product \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\), we need to find the coefficients \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\) of the resulting polynomial \\(ax^3 + bx^2 + cx + d\\). We will expand the product step-by-step.\n\nFirst, distribute each term in the first polynomial to each term in the second polynomial:\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2(7 - 2x) - 5x(7 - 2x) + 4(7 - 2x).\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term individually:\n\\[\n3x^2(7 - 2x) = 21x^2 - 6x^3,\n\\]\n\\[\n-5x(7 - 2x) = -35x + 10x^2,\n\\]\n\\[\n4(7 - 2x) = 28 - 8x.\n\\]\n\nNow, combine all these terms:\n\\[\n21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x.\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28.\n\\]\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28.\n\\]\n\nSo, the polynomial is:\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28.\n\\]\n\nIdentify the coefficients:\n\\[\na = -6, \\quad b = 31, \\quad c = -43, \\quad d = 28.\n\\]\n\nNext, compute \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28.\n\\]\n\nEvaluate step-by-step:\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48,\n\\]\n\\[\n4(31) = 124,\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86,\n\\]\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28 = 28.\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{28}.\n\\]",
