      "text": "The book suggests the following steps for the solution.\n1. Solve the product of the two polynomials.\n2. Find $8a + 4b + 2c + d$.\nSo, how can I determine these steps? To solve the given problem, we need to find the product of the polynomials \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\) and then identify the coefficients \\(a\\), \\(b\\), \\(c\\), and \\(d\\). Finally, we will compute \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\).\n\n### Step 1: Expand the Product\n\nFirst, we expand the polynomial \\((3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)\\). We do this using the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials).\n\n\\[\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) = 3x^2 \\cdot 7 + 3x^2 \\cdot (-2x) + (-5x) \\cdot 7 + (-5x) \\cdot (-2x) + 4 \\cdot 7 + 4 \\cdot (-2x)\n\\]\n\nNow, we perform each multiplication:\n\n\\[\n= 21x^2 - 6x^3 - 35x + 10x^2 + 28 - 8x\n\\]\n\nCombine like terms:\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + (21x^2 + 10x^2) + (-35x - 8x) + 28\n\\]\n\n\\[\n= -6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Identify the Coefficients\n\nThe expanded form of the product is:\n\n\\[\n-6x^3 + 31x^2 - 43x + 28\n\\]\n\nFrom this, we identify the coefficients:\n- \\(a = -6\\)\n- \\(b = 31\\)\n- \\(c = -43\\)\n- \\(d = 28\\)\n\n### Step 3: Compute \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\)\n\nNow, we substitute these coefficients into the expression \\(8a + 4b + 2c + d\\):\n\n\\[\n8a + 4b + 2c + d = 8(-6) + 4(31) + 2(-43) + 28\n\\]\n\nCalculate each term:\n\n\\[\n8(-6) = -48\n\\]\n\\[\n4(31) = 124\n\\]\n\\[\n2(-43) = -86\n\\]\n\\[\n28 = 28\n\\]\n\nAdd these values together:\n\n\\[\n-48 + 124 - 86 + 28 = 18\n\\]\n\nThus, the final answer is:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{18}\n\\]",
