      "text": "Method 1:\nStep 1: Expand $(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x)$.\n\\begin{align*}\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) &= (3x^2 + 6x^3 - 10x^3 - 20x^2 + 24x - 16x + 32) \\\\\n&= 6x^3 - 56x^2 + 8x + 32\n\\end{align*}\n\nStep 2: Identify $a, b, c, d$.\nFrom the expanded form, we have:\n$$a = 6, b = -56, c = 8, d = 32$$\n\nStep 3: Compute $8a + 4b + 2c + d$.\n\\begin{align*}\n8a + 4b + 2c + d &= 8(6) + 4(-56) + 2(8) + 32 \\\\\n&= 48 - 224 + 16 + 32 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{-130}\n\\end{align*}\n\n---\n\nMethod 2:\nStep 1: Factor out the greatest common coefficient between terms in $a$:\n\\begin{align*}\n(3x^2 - 5x + 4)(7 - 2x) &= (3x^2 + 2)(-2x^2 - 3x + 7)\n\\end{align*}\n\\begin{align*}\n(-3x^2 - 6x + 7)(-2x^2 - 3x + 7)\n\\end{align*}\n\nStep 2: Apply the FOIL method:\n\\begin{align*}\nx_1x_1 &= (3x^2)(-3x^2) + (3x^2)(-x^2) + (3x^2)(7) &+ (-5x)(-3x^2) + (-5x)(-x^2) + (-5x)(7) \\\\\n&+ (4)(-3x^2) + (4)(-x^2) + (4)(7) \\\\\n&= -9x^4 - 3x^4 + 21x^2 - (15x^3 - 5x^2) - 35x + 12x^2 + 28 \\\\\n&= -9x^4 - 15x^3 + 28x^2 - 35x + 12x^2 + 28 \\\\\n&= -34x^4 - 15x^3 + 40x^2 - 35x + 28\n\\end{align*}\n\nStep 3: Relate this result to the original expression and compute $8a + 4b + 2c + d$.\n\\begin{align*}\n8a + 4b + 2c + d &= 8(-34) + 4(-15) + 2(40) + 28 \\\\\n&= \\boxed{-34}\n\\end{align*}",
